  "step_2": "The individual describes uncovering outcomes from 'top left to bottom left, then top right to bottom right,' which suggests a visual presentation of the lotteries was used, but this detail does not affect the content of the reasoning. The key part of the verbal report is: 'Ich nutze lieber mein Glück zu 50% nichts zu verlieren als ganz sicher 500€ zu verlieren' — 'I'd rather use my luck to have a 50% chance of losing nothing than surely lose 500€.' This indicates that the individual considered the certainty of losing 500€ in Lottery A versus the chance of avoiding a loss in Lottery B. The individual values the possibility of avoiding a loss (i.e., the 50% chance of losing nothing) more than accepting a sure loss. Thus, the individual focused on the probability of avoiding a loss (or equivalently, the probability of incurring a loss) as a key factor in the decision.",
